('f15b323e-53be-5461-91f7-dd92482f4dba'::uuid,'est','"Functions, Transformations & Graphs"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"Which graph best represents −5y = −6x + 15?\n[Figure: four grids. A: line through (0,3) and (2.5,0) falling. B: line through (0,−3) and (−2.5,0) falling. C: line through (0,−3) and (2.5,0) rising. D: line through (0,3) and (−2.5,0) rising.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"Graph A"},{"key":"B","text":"Graph B"},{"key":"C","text":"Graph C"},{"key":"D","text":"Graph D"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-07","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Functions, Transformations & Graphs"}'::jsonb,'"C"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-07)."'::jsonb),
('1924344e-424a-5a48-9223-33516fc7e451'::uuid,'est','"Polynomials & Quadratic Functions"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"A baker determined the annual profit in dollars from selling pies using p(n) = 52n − 0.05n², where n is the number of pies sold. What is the annual profit if the baker sells 400 pies?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"$20,780"},{"key":"G","text":"$12,800"},{"key":"H","text":"$28,800"},{"key":"J","text":"$20,760"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-08","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Polynomials & Quadratic Functions"}'::jsonb,'"G"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-08)."'::jsonb),
