('d77748df-2be1-589e-ad4e-7319c8b6efb2'::uuid,'est','"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"What is the equation in slope-intercept form of the line that crosses the x-axis at 36 and is perpendicular to the line represented by y = −(4/9)x + 5?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"y = (4/9)x + 16"},{"key":"G","text":"y = (4/9)x − 16"},{"key":"H","text":"y = (9/4)x + 81"},{"key":"J","text":"y = (9/4)x − 81"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-10","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Coordinate Geometry, Circles & Conics"}'::jsonb,'"J"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-10)."'::jsonb),
('0beb1837-27ff-5288-b627-55dc57b44af1'::uuid,'est','"Functions, Transformations & Graphs"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"[Figure: \"Student''s Workout\" — line from (0, 100) to (50, 0); y = percentage remaining, x = minutes.]\nA student worked out at a gym continuously for 50 minutes. The graph shows the remaining percentage of the workout as a linear function of x, the time in minutes. Which answer choice best describes the domain and range of the function for this situation?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"Domain: all real numbers ≥ 0 and ≤ 100; Range: all real numbers ≥ 0 and ≤ 50"},{"key":"B","text":"Domain: {−2}; Range: {100}"},{"key":"C","text":"Domain: all real numbers ≥ 0 and ≤ 50; Range: all real numbers ≥ 0 and ≤ 100"},{"key":"D","text":"Domain: {100}; Range: {−2}"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-11","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Functions, Transformations & Graphs"}'::jsonb,'"C"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-11)."'::jsonb),
