('f87b39be-3fe5-5a5e-9d50-04768ad524b0'::uuid,'est','"Rational, Radical, Exponential & Logarithmic Functions"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"Which expression is equivalent to (45m⁻⁶p²v¹²)/(15m⁻²p⁸v⁻⁴) for all values of m, p, and v where the expression is defined?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"3v⁸/(m⁸p⁶)"},{"key":"B","text":"3v¹⁶/(m⁴p⁶)"},{"key":"C","text":"30m³/(p⁴v³)"},{"key":"D","text":"30v³/(m³p⁴)"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-13","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Rational, Radical, Exponential & Logarithmic Functions"}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-13)."'::jsonb),
('a8d4c494-4484-5933-a2b0-bfca0dd2ff58'::uuid,'est','"Solid Geometry & Volume"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"[Figure: Sphere with diameter 15 in. marked across the center.]\nA sphere and its dimension are shown in the diagram. Which measurement is closest to the volume of the sphere in cubic inches?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"1,325.4 in.³"},{"key":"G","text":"188.5 in.³"},{"key":"H","text":"94.2 in.³"},{"key":"J","text":"1,767.1 in.³"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-14","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Solid Geometry & Volume"}'::jsonb,'"J"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-14)."'::jsonb),
('70fec550-f922-5420-83f8-b3fd72cd5bc8'::uuid,'est','"Polynomials & Quadratic Functions"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"Which expression is equivalent to (10 + 7r − r²) + (−6r² − 18 + 5r)?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"−7r² + 2r + 8"},{"key":"G","text":"7r² + 12r + 8"},{"key":"H","text":"−7r² + 12r − 8"},{"key":"J","text":"7r² + 2r − 8"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-15","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Polynomials & Quadratic Functions"}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-15)."'::jsonb),
('7a8e44b4-1eba-5556-b982-57a9046e6f15'::uuid,'est','"Solid Geometry & Volume"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"Which graph best represents the solution set of y > 3x − 4?\n[Figure: four grids. A: solid line slope 3 through (0,−4), shaded below-right. B: solid line slope 3, shaded above. C: dashed line slope 3, shaded below. D: dashed line slope 3 through (0,−4), shaded above.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"Graph A"},{"key":"B","text":"Graph B"},{"key":"C","text":"Graph C"},{"key":"D","text":"Graph D"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-17","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Solid Geometry & Volume"}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-17)."'::jsonb),
('082fc736-e831-51c7-ad14-48e514ac8394'::uuid,'est','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'easy','mcq','"A bank account earning annual compound interest was opened, and no additional deposits or withdrawals were made after the initial deposit. The balance in the account after x years can be modeled by b(x) = 850(1.025)ˣ. Which statement is the best interpretation of one of the values in this function?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"The initial balance of the account decreases at a rate of 97.5% each year."},{"key":"G","text":"The balance in the account increases at a rate of 2.5% each year."},{"key":"H","text":"The initial balance of the account was $1,025."},{"key":"J","text":"The balance in the account at the end of one year is $850."}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-18","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"}'::jsonb,'"G"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-18)."'::jsonb),
('83bd4561-21e0-577a-a6d7-4354b02adf26'::uuid,'est','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'easy','mcq','"A company collected data for the number of text messages sent and received using a text-message application since October 2011. The table shows the number of text messages sent and received in billions over time. The data can be modeled by a quadratic function.\nMonths since Oct 2011, t: 5, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30, 35, 40\nMessages n(t) (billions): 3, 10, 17, 27, 44, 64, 86, 112\nWhich function best models the data?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"n(t) = −0.002t² + 0.55t + 5.02"},{"key":"B","text":"n(t) = 0.072t² − 0.15t + 2.73"},{"key":"C","text":"n(t) = −0.002t² + 5.02"},{"key":"D","text":"n(t) = 0.072t² + 2.73"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-19","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-19)."'::jsonb),
('171a3aa4-329b-5722-a367-00957e02fa5a'::uuid,'est','"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"[Figure: Two similar hexagons. Figure I: vertices R, S, T, U, V, W (R marked with double arc, T and V with single arcs). Figure II: vertices A, B, C, D, E, F (F single arc, B single arc, D double arc).]\nFigure I and Figure II are similar figures. Which proportion must be true?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"RS/AB = TU/CD"},{"key":"G","text":"TU/AB = UV/AF"},{"key":"H","text":"ST/EF = WR/CD"},{"key":"J","text":"WV/AB = ST/EF"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-20","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"}'::jsonb,'"H"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-20)."'::jsonb),
