('4048e356-9602-5ae1-b468-8ae1fded6d68'::uuid,'est','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'easy','mcq','"A company advertises on a website. A worker tracked the number of visits to the website and the number of clicks on the advertisement. The table shows the data for several days. A linear function can be used to model the data.\nVisits x: 153, 629, 471, 914, 307, 1045, 510, 1106\nClicks y: 14, 38, 30, 53, 21, 60, 32, 63\nBased on the table, what is the best prediction of the number of clicks on the advertisement if 1,500 people visit the website?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"77"},{"key":"G","text":"137"},{"key":"H","text":"83"},{"key":"J","text":"105"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-22","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"}'::jsonb,'"H"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-22)."'::jsonb),
