('fa4f1b8a-aa64-5a17-ae36-c2cb7bb5a237'::uuid,'est','"Sequences, Complex Numbers & Advanced Algebra"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"A college student has two different jobs. Her combined work schedules consist of no more than 48 hours in one week. Which graph best represents the solution set for all possible combinations of x, the number of hours she worked at her first job, and y, the number of hours she worked at her second job, in one week?\n[Figure: four \"Work Schedule\" grids. A: line from (0,48) to (48,0), shaded below the line. B: line from (0,48) to (48,0), shaded above. C: line from (0,0) to (54,54), shaded above. D: line from (0,0) to (54,54), shaded below.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"Graph A"},{"key":"B","text":"Graph B"},{"key":"C","text":"Graph C"},{"key":"D","text":"Graph D"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-47","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Sequences, Complex Numbers & Advanced Algebra"}'::jsonb,'"A"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-47)."'::jsonb),
('1b858a48-a692-57c6-ab21-94870f985bf5'::uuid,'est','"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"Which function is equivalent to q(x) = 9x² − 24x + 16?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"q(x) = (9x − 4)(x − 4)"},{"key":"G","text":"q(x) = (3x + 4)²"},{"key":"H","text":"q(x) = (9x + 4)(x + 4)"},{"key":"J","text":"q(x) = (3x − 4)²"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-48","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"}'::jsonb,'"J"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-48)."'::jsonb),
('458c716a-99fc-5017-9ebb-abe3cd417304'::uuid,'est','"Functions, Transformations & Graphs"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"Which graph best represents this system of equations and its solution?\n8x − 4y = −16\n3x + 15y = −6\n[Figure: four grids, each with a steep line and a shallow line. A: steep rising line through (0,4)-region and shallow falling line, crossing near (2,…) — no. B: steep rising line and shallow falling line crossing at (−2, 0). C: steep falling line and shallow rising line crossing near (−1,−3). D: steep falling line and shallow rising line crossing near (0, 2).]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"Graph A"},{"key":"B","text":"Graph B"},{"key":"C","text":"Graph C"},{"key":"D","text":"Graph D"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t8.md","source_sha256":"8f03df34fa98881a0531e925df7d2a108b1590182b68af8e273abe0930b44cfb","source_question_id":"T8-49","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Functions, Transformations & Graphs"}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t8.md (T8-49)."'::jsonb),
