('35e54358-35a4-581e-9753-05b46373b13c'::uuid,'est','"Sequences, Complex Numbers & Advanced Algebra"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"The entire graph of a function, F, is shown in the standard (x,y) coordinate plane below. One of the following sets is the range of the function. Which set is it?\n[Figure: discrete points at approximately (0, 6), (1, 4), (2, 2), (3, 0), (4, 2), (5, 4), (6, 6).]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"{y: y ≥ 0}"},{"key":"B","text":"{y: 0 ≤ y ≤ 6}"},{"key":"C","text":"{x: 0 ≤ x ≤ 6}"},{"key":"D","text":"{0, 2, 4, 6}"},{"key":"E","text":"{0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t9.md","source_sha256":"417d165758ab4ea90b91891cea0b6cd71d4ad113c1cbac2ccd7241a361c29d57","source_question_id":"T9-19","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Sequences, Complex Numbers & Advanced Algebra"}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t9.md (T9-19)."'::jsonb),
